# Mohawk street scene — character references

When generating or extending Mohawk **street / lifestyle** art (crowd shots, hero plates, reels):

**Face policy:** never show recognizable faces unless the user explicitly requests faces — see `mohawk-marketing-assets.mdc`.

## Mohawk figure

- Man with **black mohawk**, tight black clothes, **black jacket** (leather or similar) with **small patches**.
- Often **softened by vapor, steam, or haze** in crowd shots; may read sharper when he is a focal foreground figure.

## Reference female model 1

- Long **blonde wavy hair**.
- **Tight short black dress** (thin straps).
- Default footwear in hero / night street: **black high heels**. Shoe studies also use **red heels**, **white heels**, or **red-white Converse high tops**.

## Reference female model 2

- Long **straight dark brown hair** (not curly).
- **Brown or tan jacket/vest** over **short black skirt**, **patterned lace leggings or stockings**.
- Default footwear in hero: **dark boots**. Same shoe studies as model 1: **red heels**, **white heels**, or **Converse high tops**.

## Composition modes

- **Together:** walking away from camera side by side (Mohawk hero, early model-ref plates).
- **Split frame:** both in one shot, **not together** — separated in space, **different activities** (see `models-ref-split-*.jpg`).

## Canonical Mohawk static hero

- **File:** `Site/img/mohawk-hero.jpg`
- **Source plate:** gritty neon crowd night (`mohawk-hero-gritty-street-source.jpg` in `NewTowerArtWork/img/`)
- Models 1 & 2 appear in the **center mid-ground** of this hero; Mohawk figure **foreground right**. (Hero still shows model 2 with earlier curly-hair plate until re-shot.)

## Setting notes

- Night, dense crowd, traffic, neon, steam — see gritty-street studies in `NewTowerArtWork/img/gritty-street/` when needed.
- **Model-ref plates:** `Site/img/models-ref/` — together (`models-ref-daylight`, `-bar`, `-bookstore`); split + shoes (`models-ref-split-red-heels`, `-white-heels`, `-converse`). Archives in `NewTowerArtWork/img/models-ref/`.
- Distant **stone obelisk tower** optional in other plates; hero is **street-only** (no tower required in frame).
